{"name":"Pyramid","hex":"#9f7d4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pyramid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A solitaire card game where the cards are arranged as a triangle (a \"pyramid\") and the object is to get the cards from the bottom to the top."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pyramid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pyramid","blocks":[{"text":"A pyramid is a structure whose visible surfaces are triangular in broad outline and converge toward the top, making the appearance roughly a pyramid in the geometric sense. The base of a pyramid can be of any polygon shape, such as triangular or quadrilateral, and its surface-lines either filled or stepped."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/01_khafre_north.jpg/330px-01_khafre_north.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid"},{"title":"Pyramid (game show)","blocks":[{"text":"Pyramid is an American game show franchise that has aired several versions domestically and internationally. The show was developed by Bob Stewart. The original series, The $10,000 Pyramid, debuted on CBS on March 26, 1973, and spawned seven subsequent Pyramid series. Most later series featured a full title format matching the original series, with the title reflecting an increasing top prize. Two teams, each consisting of a celebrity and contestant, attempt to convey mystery words and phrases within a common category, against a time limit, to win cash and prizes. The title refers to the show's pyramid-shaped gameboard, featuring six categories arranged in a triangular fashion. The various Pyramid series have won a total of nine Daytime Emmys for Outstanding Game Show, second only to Jeopardy!, which has won 13."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4c/Pyramid_2017_logo.png/330px-Pyramid_2017_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_(game_show)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Koh_Ker_temple%282007%29.jpg/500px-Koh_Ker_temple%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Koh_Ker_temple%282007%29.jpg/500px-Koh_Ker_temple%282007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prasat Thom temple at Koh Ker, Cambodia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoh_Ker_temple(2007).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg/500px-White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg/1280px-White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg/500px-White_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_Temple_ziggurat_in_Uruk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/The_White_Temple_%27E_at_Uruk%2C_3500-3000_BCE.jpg/500px-The_White_Temple_%27E_at_Uruk%2C_3500-3000_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/The_White_Temple_%27E_at_Uruk%2C_3500-3000_BCE.jpg/500px-The_White_Temple_%27E_at_Uruk%2C_3500-3000_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_White_Temple_'E_at_Uruk%2C_3500-3000_BCE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Choghazanbil2.